  "question": {
    "text": "White phosphorus on reaction with concentrated <math> <mrow> <mtext>NaOH</mtext></mrow> </math> solution in an inert atmosphere of <math><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> gives phosphine and compound <math> <mrow> <mtext>(X)</mtext></mrow> </math>. <math> <mrow> <mtext>(X)</mtext></mrow> </math> on acidification with <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> gives compound <math> <mrow> <mtext>(Y)</mtext></mrow> </math>. The basicity of compound <math> <mrow> <mtext>(Y)</mtext></mrow> </math> is",
